e":"746.1309(d)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-07-25","finding":"Documented Annual Training - Caregivers of Children Under 24 Months Required: One caregiver did not have current training for children under 24 months of age. This caregiver was caring for infants in the 0-11 month old room.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026363911","violation_type_title":"Documented Annual Training - Caregivers of Children Under 24 Months Required (26 TAC §746.1309(d))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-355342-i20250724-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-355342-i20250724","date":"2025-07-24","original_code":"746.3701","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-08-01","finding":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards: 1.A TV that was mounted on the wall had an extension cord which was accessible to the children in care. The cord could be pulled, making the equipment fall on a  child. The cords must be made inaccessible to the children in care.         2.The fence, around the outdoor playground, was observed to have an area that was not attached to the ground. This caused a hole that a child could gain access.  The fence must be repaired to make this area inaccessible.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026243332","violation_type_title":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards (26 TAC §746.3701)","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-355342-i20250724-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-12","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-355342-i20250724","date":"2025-07-24","original_code":"746.3407(12)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Mark Cleaning Supplies, Toxic Materials; Keep Separate from Food and Inaccessible to Children: The bottles used for cleaning were not marked w